        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under a dry oxygen-free N2 atmosphere (Schlenk), Zn(NO3)2·6H2O (0.20 mmol, 0.0441 g), Sm(OAc)3·4H2O (0.20 mmol, 0.0842 g) and H2L (0.20 mmol, 0.0888 g) were dissolved in 15 mL of MeOH/EtOH (1:2) at room temperature, then Et3N in EtOH (0.35 mol L−1, 2 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred and refluxed for 30 min, cooled, and filtered. Diethyl ether was allowed to diffuse slowly into the filtrate at room temperature; pale yellow crystals formed after one month, were filtered, washed with EtOH (5 mL), and dried in air for one week.",
